  "id": "cmgiswmgi0032iae0c9606lxd",
  "slug": "megaplex",
  "name": "Megaplex",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Megaplex is an annual furry convention in Florida, first held March 8 to 10, 2002, as Pawpet Megaplex. It began as a replacement for Furry Spring Break and was organized by Pawpet Live Experiences, Inc., and it is now run by Florida United Furry Fandom, Inc. (FLUFF). Programming has centered on fursuiting, puppetry, improvisation and other performance, with musical acts such as Toxic Audio, 4:2:Five, Matthew Ebel, Fox Amoore and Rhubarb the Bear, stage musicals such as Julie Bunny Must Die! and Fosgate: Ferret Loan Officer, and out-of-fandom guests such as Trace Beaulieu, Paul Zaloom and Noel MacNeal. The convention introduced a convention fursuit mascot, Pounce the Panther, in 2008, has made a commemorative poster each year since 2012, and has streamed its main events online since 2005. It moved from Orlando to Jacksonville for two years and then returned to the Orlando area, and since 2023 it has been held at the Hyatt Regency Orlando. Its charity partner was the C.A.R.E. Foundation, an animal rescue, until 2023, and attendance has grown steadily since 2010 to 12,522 in 2026.",
